Package: kichat
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Kai Stadtmueller <kai.stadtmueller@live.de>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1-0, libsoup-3.0-0, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0
Description: Local-first LLM research chat
 KiChat talks to a language model running on your own machine (LM Studio,
 Ollama, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) and searches the web through Brave
 or DuckDuckGo when a question needs current information: prices, laws, news,
 live data. Attached documents are extracted and indexed locally, long
 conversations are compacted automatically before they overflow the context
 window, and every chat lives in a SQLite database under ~/.config/kichat.
 There is no account, no cloud and no telemetry, and the network is only used
 for the searches and model calls you ask for.
